From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niravkumar L Rabara <niravkumarlaxmidas.rabara@altera.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] cpu_init: _stack_setup: skip EL2/EL0 stacks under HV_GUEST_EL1

MSR SP_EL1 is only writable from EL2+; executed from EL1 it is
UNDEFINED, not a trap to EL2 - the exception lands right back in the
guest's own sync-exception vector, which just spins under Bao, before
the UART is usable.

Under HV_GUEST_EL1 install the EL1 stack top - the slot a hypervisor at
EL2 would have handed down to EL1 - directly on the current SP. Keeping
the same per-core slot layout means the _STACK_EL012 / _STACK_MAX
arithmetic in lscript.ld is identical for guest and bare-metal builds.

SP_EL0 is deliberately left untouched here (the bare-metal #else branch
still pre-seeds it). MSR SP_EL0 from EL1 is legal, but nothing reads it
before FreeRTOS's own portRESTORE_CONTEXT loads it from the first
task's TCB when the scheduler starts, so a value written here would
never be observed. Restoring that write for strict EL0/EL1/EL2 parity
with the bare-metal path is deferred to a follow-up change.

Ported from patches/v26.1-SMP/0006, which patched the duplicated stack
pre-seed in _boot and _secondary_boot. v26.3 factored both copies into a
single _stack_setup routine, so this is now one hunk instead of two.

Signed-off-by: Niravkumar L Rabara <niravkumarlaxmidas.rabara@altera.com>
---
diff --git a/FreeRTOS/Demo/SOCFPGA/startup/cpu_init.S b/FreeRTOS/Demo/SOCFPGA/startup/cpu_init.S
index a4773f5..226bcde 100644
--- a/FreeRTOS/Demo/SOCFPGA/startup/cpu_init.S
+++ b/FreeRTOS/Demo/SOCFPGA/startup/cpu_init.S
@@ -117,6 +117,27 @@ _stack_setup:
     ldr x0, =_STACK_START
     ldr x1, =_STACK_EL012
     msub x0, x1, x3, x0      /* x0 = __stack_top - (_STACK_EL012 * core_id) */
+#ifdef HV_GUEST_EL1
+    /* A hypervisor guest enters directly at EL1, so the only legal target
+     * for this routine is the current EL1 stack pointer. MSR SP_EL1 from
+     * EL1 is UNDEFINED (that register is only writable from EL2+); on Bao
+     * the resulting exception is taken right back into this guest's own
+     * sync-exception vector, which just spins (b .), so the symptom reads
+     * like a hang rather than a trap to the hypervisor.
+     *
+     * We deliberately leave SP_EL0 untouched here (unlike the bare-metal
+     * path below, which pre-seeds it). MSR SP_EL0 from EL1 is legal, but
+     * nothing reads SP_EL0 before FreeRTOS's own portRESTORE_CONTEXT loads
+     * it from the first task's TCB when the scheduler starts, so a
+     * pre-seeded value here would never be observed. Install the EL1
+     * stack top -- the slot a guest at EL2 would have handed down to EL1
+     * -- on the current SP. Keeping the same slot layout means the memory
+     * map in lscript.ld is unchanged between guest and bare-metal builds. */
+    /* EL1 top = EL2 top - EL2 size */
+    ldr x1, =_EL2_STACK_SIZE
+    sub x0, x0, x1
+    mov sp, x0
+#else
     /* EL2 top */
     mov sp, x0
     /* EL1 top = EL2 top - EL2 size */
@@ -127,6 +148,7 @@ _stack_setup:
     ldr x1, =_EL1_STACK_SIZE
     sub x0, x0, x1
     msr sp_el0, x0
+#endif
 
     ret
 
